[[:db/retract 17592186229658 :question/answer-fields 17592186228148] [:db/retract 17592186229658 :question/answer-fields 17592186228138] [:db/retract 17592186229658 :question/answer-fields 17592186228143] [:db/retract 17592186311078 :answer-field/choices 17592186310704] [:db/retract 17592186310956 :answer-field/choices 17592186310560] {:db/id 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-964cfe5a-540f-5a2a-90eb-038dd13a228b" "question-4daa880b-394e-5da4-a6f8-c7b8b600dc37" "question-232a3dab-08a5-5200-8a90-246a69a099b3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228910 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to the system of ODEs above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/4c/4c7ca8aa3fb83e7c4ce806080257e8f3b3d5186e19f10649a0bed7202f6501b6.svg) where ![](images/04/0492dd33f8d39d4a74139be25415d6d943888d8ccbf67158690f0960c5334415.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/85/85304407fca2ace2d7fb5d97123e1f27f45386c8f3ebcc1a1c3859d1b573d2b0.svg)\nwhere ![](images/81/81bcc770826e2156f310569f014356cc686541259c11aa190ac28394a6d38725.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/31/310669815cad029379ffa4022fa9094ef8597d91496c57f70c66ed51926836b3.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n![](images/e1/e128d7d4610a3a9021b1391f278822bcdf113570500b822c05370e473923f5b7.svg)\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} & t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ {e}^{-7t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5d3d32e6-9123-5862-a54d-5cd0459cabee" "question-32d4b06d-f6f3-5351-bf77-6d5871dae39c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228918 :question/problem "![](images/6e/6e456b14ca5110a5cf290cd0053bd52652c8d44e2e9f517f73d2b257c355b8cf.svg)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/e4/e43485cd9eaca81dd04089924a83a909594e575d76d195850cf11719809acbbd.svg) where ![](images/6a/6ac1e35cee6cfbab9771278c3a68f422e5422ef79e4f516755e35748ea402e08.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/b4/b434d5c8a601c3d7fae734a5b78437457fab7877fe0ca1ff466197817d9d1c0e.svg)\nwhere ![](images/cc/cc9313ae17390c751e51673c53d788c24308f501fa7107e3098cd370028eb1d2.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/1d/1d3df45727a13bfbc41ab2689fd1a9a6dbcc28fd4ed071a430a2e745e99aeec8.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{x}(0),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{x}(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n![](images/a9/a998751dcfc2e8acb4e142c5b4a5241ec61fe3bc087dccf9fe87344d73b04ce3.svg)\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e674cbe1-254a-5d93-a9b4-be22a2029aaf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228917 :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0d7ecb854b93b475f1897f7ae66e0e459a5ad22247a9d9a5c11adff32b747e4.svg)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/50/50c3d207258cc321a19532b7b54da568a4a6361dde55f35247fe60e931fe5f93.svg) where ![](images/59/599d579a41d84635ae3a34867759b69af6b406d433c4c11a53898f69e856371e.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/6d/6dfab7c1edb51450a9238b3fd1154c7d4a5dccb47c689c54768c4b6cc952c068.svg)\nwhere ![](images/eb/eb99201c10627a06594c4967ac8f3a56cb75784f1f824332a9b58a10aaf672bc.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/e7/e70ec908edd1985f4f1f719dceee192536c0bcdf0b4deedcf1c9f785005ee041.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\mathbf{c} =e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t = t_0,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0) = e^{At_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nand since $e^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c} = e^{-At_0} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $\\mathbf{x}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7ee364d4-3865-58d1-b13b-994e56af1ccf" "question-c3c2f127-8fe3-52c5-8ea9-fa818612f56c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186228911 :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t) = A\\Phi_0(t), \\qquad \\Phi_0(0) = I_n.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ passing through $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\textrm{L1}{:}\\;$ Let $\\Phi_0(t)=e^{At}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L2}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=\\Phi_0(t)\\,\\mathbf{c}$ for some constant vector $\\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L3}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At}\\,\\mathbf{c}$ \n\n$\\textrm{L4}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L5}{:}\\;$ $(e^{A t_0})^{-1} \\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1} e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c}$  \n\n$\\textrm{L6}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{c} = e^{-A t_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L7}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} e^{-At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L8}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At - At_0} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\n$\\textrm{L9}{:}\\;$ $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{A(t-t_0)} \\mathbf{x}(t_0) \\,$  \n\nFill in the blanks to justify each step of the following reasoning.\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](images/b2/b2df506469d945a843b7784f38a1b12d6f89016aee1fb12581705b6d9d98baab.svg)\n\n$\\qquad$ The property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](images/7a/7af985a90d901c63f7d03feda679d513fa18ccb36d34c8fb237ac755baf9f801.svg)\n\n$\\qquad$ Line $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that  ![](images/c5/c55c24e30a71bf93cdd21c2a5d0f3c68271cd6fb3f2033b84ce8338569eacd4a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\textrm{L4}$ and $\\textrm{L5}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L4},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=e^{A t_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwe multiply both sides on the left by $(e^{At_0})^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n(e^{A t_0})^{-1}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=(e^{At_0})^{-1}e^{A t_0}\\,\\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\textrm{L5}$ follows from $\\textrm{L4}$ by ![](images/22/2226897d3c49c80358dc93ec1d1d80bd8b513764e6b39bbf93408215c83144bf.svg)\n\n- Next, we justify the step $\\textrm{L7}$ to $\\textrm{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-At_0$ commute, we may combine exponentials:\n\n$$\ne^{At}e^{-At_0}=e^{At-At_0}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\textrm{L7}$ produces line $\\textrm{L8}.$ Hence, the property of the matrix exponential used in $\\textrm{L8}$ is ![](images/e4/e4a1c6f6b74ea7491973a3bfa76225f1f6af67a681582a49afa51772c05bfaed.svg)\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\textrm{L8}$ and $\\textrm{L9}.$ Starting from $\\textrm{L8},$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{At-At_0}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-At_0=A(t-t_0)$ to get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t)=e^{A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\textrm{L9}.$ Thus, $\\textrm{L9}$ follows from $\\textrm{L8}$ by the fact that $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt lightgray]{At-At_0=A(t-t_0)\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }t_0}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-964cfe5a-540f-5a2a-90eb-038dd13a228b" :question/id #uuid "964cfe5a-540f-5a2a-90eb-038dd13a228b" :question/math-academy-id "q-334778" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-6x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d08bec31-d229-5948-b097-4d0df5e00ec6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d08bec31-d229-5948-b097-4d0df5e00ec6" :answer-field/id #uuid "d08bec31-d229-5948-b097-4d0df5e00ec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-78df560a-fa85-549b-b255-86f7ab415d05" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d56c2436-b44b-5b68-adea-27e2397d0ff4" "answer-78df560a-fa85-549b-b255-86f7ab415d05" "answer-ec69783d-87bb-509c-94b8-4b2db9acc468" "answer-224adb82-b3c8-52f2-b2a6-c9f7f9772557" "answer-7dc2c6d7-54ef-53d5-a2b9-59e64b6ad531"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d56c2436-b44b-5b68-adea-27e2397d0ff4" :answer/id #uuid "d56c2436-b44b-5b68-adea-27e2397d0ff4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78df560a-fa85-549b-b255-86f7ab415d05" :answer/id #uuid "78df560a-fa85-549b-b255-86f7ab415d05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec69783d-87bb-509c-94b8-4b2db9acc468" :answer/id #uuid "ec69783d-87bb-509c-94b8-4b2db9acc468" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-224adb82-b3c8-52f2-b2a6-c9f7f9772557" :answer/id #uuid "224adb82-b3c8-52f2-b2a6-c9f7f9772557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7dc2c6d7-54ef-53d5-a2b9-59e64b6ad531" :answer/id #uuid "7dc2c6d7-54ef-53d5-a2b9-59e64b6ad531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186308684 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=6x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=6y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].$*" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229677 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-4daa880b-394e-5da4-a6f8-c7b8b600dc37" :question/id #uuid "4daa880b-394e-5da4-a6f8-c7b8b600dc37" :question/math-academy-id "q-334765" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0f0167e8-c854-5755-b6be-76017465421b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0f0167e8-c854-5755-b6be-76017465421b" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f0167e8-c854-5755-b6be-76017465421b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bdf2a9b4-44d2-5fb1-9e1f-8e147e929ada" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8524af80-eac0-5f3d-ba4c-7130ca74bc3b" "answer-613c735f-5122-5927-a809-bc329b4307b2" "answer-bdf2a9b4-44d2-5fb1-9e1f-8e147e929ada" "answer-dfd5e439-6415-5c58-b198-adfa34053c47" "answer-2cade7c7-d983-59b8-9669-6f8e3582aaa2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8524af80-eac0-5f3d-ba4c-7130ca74bc3b" :answer/id #uuid "8524af80-eac0-5f3d-ba4c-7130ca74bc3b" :answer/type :