ing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3ef25a83-ddcb-554d-87b8-5aa072e19c0a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3ef25a83-ddcb-554d-87b8-5aa072e19c0a" :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef25a83-ddcb-554d-87b8-5aa072e19c0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5fdffc17-8494-5d04-aeb1-07a8cd779b34" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d7bb90c-0a41-5654-826b-4c1b3874378f" "answer-5fdffc17-8494-5d04-aeb1-07a8cd779b34" "answer-15e54b7e-2eb9-5c30-98bc-552eced01142" "answer-9d4acd53-73d9-572f-9114-3eb8d8cd79ac" "answer-1946