:db/id "answer-81738d4b-ad6c-5c58-9652-7aa7295f8d23" :answer/id #uuid "81738d4b-ad6c-5c58-9652-7aa7295f8d23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sin(8(t+1))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186310951 :answer-field/correct "answer-f947e9b5-78ea-57fb-a267-4b7bbb84d360" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f947e9b5-78ea-57fb-a267-4b7bbb84d360"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f947e9b5-78ea-57fb-a267-4b7bbb84d360" :answer/id #uuid "f947e9b5-78ea-57fb-a267-4b7bbb84d360" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\cos(8(t+1))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311591 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-3) \\\\ y(-3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7t} & t{e}^{7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311031 :answer-field/correct "answer-7e39c819-e178-5bfa-a5fb-cd7dfa304efa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e39c819-e178-5bfa-a5fb-cd7dfa304efa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e39c819-e178-5bfa-a5fb-cd7dfa304efa" :answer/id #uuid "7e39c819-e178-5bfa-a5fb-cd7dfa304efa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2(t+3)e^{7(t+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311149 :answer-field/correct "answer-c4391037-0726-5baa-bba4-61f44fdba73c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4391037-0726-5baa-bba4-61f44fdba73c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4391037-0726-5baa-bba4-61f44fdba73c" :answer/id #uuid "c4391037-0726-5baa-bba4-61f44fdba73c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2e^{7(t+3)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311593 :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186311078 :answer-field/correct 17592186310072 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186310956 :answer-field/correct 17592186309902 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-7ee364d4-3865-58d1-b13b-994e56af1ccf" :question/id #uuid "7ee364d4-3865-58d1-b13b-994e56af1ccf" :question/math-academy-id "q-336478" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe evaluate both sides at $t=0$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L3}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ By definition, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ satisfies the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nThe second condition here is exactly line $\\text{L4},$ so $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by $\\text{using the initial condition }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we know\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we have ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}\\text{ into }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d4c70b5-34be-574c-b5b7-72ba11d43aed" "answer-field-03707618-f14e-58a8-b61e-58402bebc2e4" "answer-field-4c50b68d-36e9-56fe-9509-8e8268c5ac1d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d4c70b5-34be-574c-b5b7-72ba11d43aed" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d4c70b5-34be-574c-b5b7-72ba11d43aed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9b37cc40-53e5-53