:answer.type/text :answer/value "computing $det({Φ}_{0}(0))$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d439ffd-235d-5190-afa9-6f42b5a7e416" :answer/id #uuid "5d439ffd-235d-5190-afa9-6f42b5a7e416" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ at $t=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43014d39-1648-53c0-98f9-6f05e38e18a4" :answer/id #uuid "43014d39-1648-53c0-98f9-6f05e38e18a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4c50b68d-36e9-56fe-9509-8e8268c5ac1d" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c50b68d-36e9-56fe-9509-8e8268c5ac1d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9082d977-8d12-5228-84ba-cc66ffcea7a5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4e2f159-86ae-5268-99e0-e7a4a0d1cdfe" "answer-1b04e893-cceb-50bf-a491-02560d0862d0" "answer-9082d977-8d12-5228-84ba-cc66ffcea7a5" "answer-c2342d48-70e2-5f9a-b3c0-ddfbb51fdb76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4e2f159-86ae-5268-99e0-e7a4a0d1cdfe" :answer/id #uuid "f4e2f159-86ae-5268-99e0-e7a4a0d1cdfe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b04e893-cceb-50bf-a491-02560d0862d0" :answer/id #uuid "1b04e893-cceb-50bf-a491-02560d0862d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "differentiating $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9082d977-8d12-5228-84ba-cc66ffcea7a5" :answer/id #uuid "9082d977-8d12-5228-84ba-cc66ffcea7a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2342d48-70e2-5f9a-b3c0-ddfbb51fdb76" :answer/id #uuid "c2342d48-70e2-5f9a-b3c0-ddfbb51fdb76" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "using properties of the determinant of ${Φ}_{0}(0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c3c2f127-8fe3-52c5-8ea9-fa818612f56c" :question/id #uuid "c3c2f127-8fe3-52c5-8ea9-fa818612f56c" :question/math-academy-id "q-337108" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ From $\\text{L2},$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nUsing $\\text{L1}$, we substitute ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ into this equation to obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L3}.$ Thus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}\\text{ into }x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L7}.$ Using line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nFrom line $\\text{L6}$, we know that $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}).$ Substituting this expression for $c$ into the formula for $x(t)$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L8}$ and $\\text{L9}.$ Starting from $\\text{L8},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwe rewrite the exponent using the algebraic identity $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ to get\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L9}.$ Thus, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L8}$ by the fact that $At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})\\text{ for any }t\\text{ and }{t}_{0}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7bf6cf21-273f-5fc7-8e49-f04141dd7829" "answer-field-9009bdd3-b5fa-53af-9a1f-8eb62e17168c" "answer-field-4d6550ee-0193-5d90-88b0-0547b0f74454"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7bf6cf21-273f-5fc7-8e49-f04141dd7829" :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf6cf21-273f-5fc7-8e49-f04141dd7829" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-392f89bd-3ea4-5013-8e2f-76a63e1ac26e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-51b7dfa5-769d-5b7a-b02a-8fd1f441048e" "answer-392f89bd-3ea4-5013-8e2f-76a63e1ac26e" "answer-1736138c-0166-5a19-97d1-c2e44c954bbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51b7dfa5-769d-5b7a-b02a-8fd1f441048e" :answer/id #uuid "51b7dfa5-769d-5b7a-b02a-8fd1f441048e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "left-multiplying $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c$ by ${e}^{-At}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-392f89bd-3ea4-5013-8e2f-76a63e1ac26e" :answer/id #uuid "392f89bd-3ea4-5013-8e2f-76a63e1ac26e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1736138c-0166-5a19-97d1-c2e44c954bbc" :answer/id #uuid "1736138c-0166-5a19-97d1-c2e44c954bbc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9009bdd3-b5fa-53af-9a1f-8eb62e17168c" :answer-field/id #uuid "9009bdd3-b5fa-53af-9a1f-8eb62e17168c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-80c7eeb8-d9f2-55c3-989a-f5d20a196afe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45b9ffd0-4ddf-56f7-8003-86fef33ee168" "answer-a86bb449-4ce2-557f-8e36-0abb31b7f9bb" "answer-80c7eeb8-d9f2-55c3-989a-f5d20a196afe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45b9ffd0-4ddf-56f7-8003-86fef33ee168" :answer/id #uuid "45b9ffd0-4ddf-56f7-8003-86fef33ee168" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ at $t=0$ and solving for $c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a86bb449-4ce2-557f-8e36-0abb31b7f9bb" :answer/id #uuid "a86bb449-4ce2-557f-8e36-0abb31b7f9bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "left-multiplying $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ by ${e}^{-At}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-80c7eeb8-d9f2-55c3-989a-f5d20a196afe" :answer/id #uuid "80c7eeb8-d9f2-55c3-989a-f5d20a196afe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d6550ee-0193-5d90-88b0-0547b0f74454" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d6550ee-0193-5d90-88b0-0547b0f74454" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e2583d7c-7080-546c-bdfe-f2917811399f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4e50b50b-4373-51d9-9375-66dc09625989" "answer-e2583d7c-7080-546c-bdfe-f2917811399f" "answer-6d7f021d-b3da-5a02-86e5-d09f4c81daf5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e50b50b-4373-51d9-9375-66dc09625989" :answer/id #uuid "4e50b50b-4373-51d9-9375-66dc09625989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A({t}_{0}-t)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2583d7c-7080-546c-bdfe-f2917811399f" :answer/id #uuid "e2583d7c-7080-546c-bdfe-f2917811399f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$At-A{t}_{0}=A(t-{t}_{0})$ for any $t$ and ${t}_{0}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d7f021d-b3da-5a02-86e5-d09f4c81daf5" :answer/id #uuid "6d7f021d-b3da-5a02-86e5-d09f4c81daf5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${e}^{X+Y}={e}^{X}{e}^{Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230188 :tutorial/content "Matrix exponentials can be used for solving homogeneous systems of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix.\n\nFor example, consider the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-5x(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/f9/f94140f8c9fe736ca7c574547658856e85d938eb08064046716be8eb1a2748de.svg)\nwhere ![](images/26/26dcf2c367c915460d09f4f38b40e4f792a06b6ab44291b4739a6935529daf89.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/90/9000e03ddf617a1e3c4e0eed5da2b846d62e3d68588b601d90643783960d17df.svg)\n\nRecall that given the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is some constant vector.\n\nSince we have already seen how to compute the standard fundamental matrix, we will not repeat the calculation here. So, computing the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system, we get\n![](images/11/11e0da79656b7f8e2c84c6c54e6dd6b54cf53cbb8e746d44dfb13329c3d2ed8f.svg)\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.$\n\n**Note:** Recall that for the general solution of the ordinary differential equation $x'(t)=ax(t),$ we have \n\n$$\nx'(t)=ax(t)\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\nx(t) = c \\, e^{at}, \n\\quad\nc \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nNow, for the general solution of the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)\n\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n\\quad\n\\mathbf{c} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n.\n$$\n\nLet's see more examples." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230193 :tutorial/content "Now, let's find the solution to the initial value problem below\n![](images/31/3111f065d441881e050417b345b34947509f175f00ebd5402963e432d013348e.svg)\n\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/5c/5c4ed0a2e9db0979e4fc0342c2e4db7c23c60cf58293a496fa661ff1c03fccde.svg)\nwhere ![](images/71/7164659247c5290544655b05943d7d998f67cb1cc3b4cc45bab0902e8059bc75.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/e3/e3f94e8ce2cc2063d469fbac2af87232cc130f788243c1507bfe9972dd4b04c1.svg)\n\nRecall that the general solution of the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is some constant vector.\n\nEvaluating both sides of $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} \\mathbf{c}$ at $t=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & ={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c \\\\ x(0) & ={e}^{A(0)}\\,c \\\\ x(0) & =I\\,c \\\\ c & =x(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to our initial value problem is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\, \\mathbf{x}(0).\n$$\n\nComputing the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system, we get\n![](images/fc/fc4e1ba16be420fbe5e53e2dbb4ee6da96c7097bbe4e117315407ec4dc65365f.svg)\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{7t} & t{e}^{7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(3-2t){e}^{7t} \\\\ -2{e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230194 :tutorial/content "Next, let's find the solution to the initial value problem \n![](images/93/93f9c58b8a9cea64ba97f43f2831336ea8d38a6fd6165211a54d2822415c1497.svg)\ngiven that ![](images/ee/ee25228bf71d1b7d9d0688af06a7f1335c252310127b403ed0ed37f7fe277c07.svg) where ![](images/3a/3a3ac9326741c0e2390a8e2f079808f0b432b740149ef4b034ffa7568dc33848.svg)\n\nWriting our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/2b/2b81cf358ffb3df49f327b63138640ac452a249f989353b521be34d531aeffd9.svg)\nwhere ![](images/11/1110f0bdbe784b21683bfb9610ca9c04e5a45755954d49a15124e530feef2002.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/47/47d8a0214e5ccdf6625a330d23003dec11cbc3a4f35cb2992df29a688963e4b2.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution is $\\mathbf{x}(t) = e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c}.$ We can determine the constant vector $\\mathbf{c}$ using the initial condition at time $t=t_0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0) = e^{At_0} \\, \\mathbf{c} \\implies \\mathbf{c} = e^{-At_0} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0),\n$$\n\nsince the inverse of $e^{At_0}$ is $e^{-At_0}.$ Plugging this back into our general solution gives the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our specific problem (with $t_0=1$) is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-1)) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186230192 :tutorial/content "Before proceeding with the next example, let's recall some important properties of matrix exponentials:\n\n1\\. *Law of Exponents:* If $A$ is a constant square matrix, then\n\n  $$\n  e^{A(t+s)} = e^{At}\\,e^{As}.\n  $$\n\n2\\. *Inverse:* For any $t,$ the matrix $e^{At}$ is invertible and \n\n  $$\n  (e^{At})^{-1} = e^{-At}.\n  $$\n\n3\\. *Identity:* For any square matrix $A,$\n\n  $$\n  e^{A\\cdot 0} = I.\n  $$\n\n4\\. *Product of exponentials:* If $A$ and $B$ commute (i.e., $AB = BA$), then\n\n  $$\n  e^{A}e^{B} = e^{A+B}.\n  $$\n\n  **Watch out!** In general, this identity is *not true* unless $A$ and $B$ commute.\n\nLet's see how these properties can be used in practice." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186229256 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
